rendering engine:
requirements/constraints:
1.x,y,z movement
2.no rotation
3.zooming
4.no obj rotation
5.expanded layers of an object are close together(in z), except when 1 is viewable to the cam and the one behind cam.
6.as objects keep on increasing in distance from main content, their size reduces. main contents are also in heirarchy. where sub explanations of an object will make that object a main content under the heirarchy of its main content. this affects size. as well.




objects will change the following propoerties by change in z dir:
1.size. by m=k/z. where k is constant.m is scale.
2.rendering sequence. where sequence of rendering objects will be zn,zn-1,zn-2...z1.
3.change of speed of object to account fov. with formula thetax=arctan(x/z). where theta is angular pos of obj relative to cam.
4.change transperency of object when z<0.25m by g=z/0.25.

